From f4eac90381907cae07cf768812569285492f41fd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: moto <j3tm0t0@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 20:21:45 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] bootwait: "Pico Z Loader" logo (power ring with Z, Orbitron
 wordmark)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Replaces the X68000-homage emblem and wordmark with an original logo:
- Emblem from the chosen SVG (viewBox 100): ring r=44 stroke 6 with a
  power-style gap at the top (MID, palette 12), stem x47-53 y0-22 and a
  filled Z polygon (LIGHT, palette 4); 88 px tall, rendered at 4x,
  pre-squashed by 1/1.125 so the ring is round on the 4:3 screen.
- Wordmark: "PICO" in Orbitron Black (white = planes 0+1, no IOCS text
  on the logo rows), "Z" in LIGHT, spaced "LOADER" in Orbitron 800 in
  DARK (palette 8, a grey-blue with >= 4.5:1 on black).
  Orbitron (SIL OFL 1.1) is fetched into driver/fonts/ (gitignored)
  only when mkbootwait.py regenerates bootwait_gen.S.
- The logo uses all 4 text planes (planes 0 and 1 stored once); the
  waiter clears all 4 planes itself at start and before the IPL /
  setting UI. Stage 2 is 13.4 KB.
- The ring pulses (palette 12) in step with the ◆ instead of the
  triangle pairs. Subtitle "Pico Z Loader ・ Raspberry Pi Pico W /
  x68kzremotedrv", title "SMB 接続待ち…".
- waiter_test.py: logo bytes in planes 0-3, ring pulse, new titles, all
  4 planes clear on hand-over; the preview renders all planes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PrGdt1XK1exBgERrMmLA1u
